        {"id":"3da420a3","elType":"widget","widgetType":"accordion","settings":{"tabs":[{"tab_title":"What is a Badri cow?","tab_content":"The Badri cow is an indigenous hill breed native to the Uttarakhand Himalayas — one of the 50 recognised indigenous cattle breeds of India. Smaller in stature than plains breeds, Badri cows graze on Himalayan alpine herbs and grasses.","_id":"43d1f6e8"},{"tab_title":"Is Badri cow ghee different from regular A2 ghee?","tab_content":"Yes. While all Badri cow ghee is A2, it comes from a specific indigenous Himalayan breed. The unique diet — Himalayan herbs, clean mountain water, natural grazing — makes this ghee rare. Think of it like single-origin coffee vs. a blend.","_id":"4a398e0c"},{"tab_title":"Is this ghee A1 or A2?","tab_content":"[FILL IN: Confirm A2 from indigenous desi / Badri cows.]","_id":"b55c5d5a"},{"tab_title":"What is the shelf life?","tab_content":"[FILL IN: 12–18 months from manufacture date stored in a cool, dry place. Add exact date from your lab report.]","_id":"5fe7e7fa"},{"tab_title":"How should I store it?","tab_content":"Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight. Do not refrigerate — ghee is shelf-stable. Always use a dry spoon.","_id":"fbf1d72b"},{"tab_title":"Does the ghee become solid in winter?","tab_content":"Yes — completely natural and a sign of purity. Solid in cold weather, liquid in warm. Both are fine to consume.","_id":"d502a5a4"},{"tab_title":"Can I return the product?","tab_content":"Returns accepted only for damaged or incorrect items within 48 hours of delivery. See our Return & Refund Policy.","_id":"977493dd"},{"tab_title":"Do you ship pan-India?","tab_content":"Yes. Delivery takes 3–7 business days depending on location. See our Shipping Policy.","_id":"3bc79b6c"}],"active_item":1,"title_color":"#2c1810","tab_active_color":"#a07850","border_color":"#e0d5c8","border_width":"1","icon_align":"right"}}
      ]}]
